            <ArticleTitle>Lumbar stabilization: a review of core concepts and current literature, part 2.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lumbar-stabilization exercise programs have become increasingly popular as a treatment for low-back pain. In this article, we outline an evidence-based medicine approach to evaluating patients for a lumbar-stabilization program. We also discuss typical clinical components of this type of program and the rationale for including these particular features based on the medical literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
